---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const contactEmail = 'luisarosteguiruizit@gmail.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Accessibility statement for the Luis Arostegui Ruiz portfolio MVP."
  pathname="/accessibility/"
>
  <section class="statement-hero" aria-labelledby="accessibility-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Release readiness</p>
    <h1 id="accessibility-heading">Accessibility</h1>
    <p>
      This portfolio is built as a static, keyboard-accessible Astro site with
      semantic HTML, visible focus styles, responsive layouts, and restrained
      motion. Accessibility validation is part of the PT-44 MVP release gate.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="statement-section" aria-labelledby="intent-heading">
    <h2 id="intent-heading">Conformance intent</h2>
    <p>
      The implemented MVP targets WCAG 2.2 Level AA for its public portfolio
      scope. Automated checks support that work, but they do not establish full
      conformance on their own.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="statement-section" aria-labelledby="review-heading">
    <h2 id="review-heading">Review scope in progress</h2>
    <p>
      The current planned review scope is the PT-44 Portfolio MVP validation
      started on August 22, 2026. Until that validation matrix is complete, the
      review remains in progress. It covers the Home, Projects, project detail,
      Experience, Accessibility, and not-found routes, plus core navigation,
      contact, CV, metadata, responsive behaviour, reduced motion, and
      production-build output.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="statement-section" aria-labelledby="limitations-heading">
    <h2 id="limitations-heading">Known limitations</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Validation is still being completed for the MVP release and combines
        automated checks with manual keyboard, screen-reader, zoom, reflow,
        motion, contrast, and content review.
      </li>
      <li>
        External tools, browsers, assistive technologies, and personal settings
        can expose issues that are not detected by automated scans.
      </li>
      <li>
        The site currently provides direct contact links instead of a contact
        form, so there are no form validation states in the MVP scope.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="statement-section" aria-labelledby="feedback-heading">
    <h2 id="feedback-heading">Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you find an accessibility barrier in this portfolio, send a note by
      email and include the page, browser, device, assistive technology if
      relevant, and what blocked the task.
    </p>
    <a class="action" href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>Send an email</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(#main-content) {
    inline-size: min(
      100% - (2 * var(--layout-gutter-mobile)),
      var(--layout-content-readable)
    );
  }

  .statement-hero,
  .statement-section {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .statement-hero {
    padding-block-end: var(--space-7);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--colour-border-subtle);
  }

  .statement-hero h1 {
    margin-block: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--type-heading-1-font-size);
    line-height: var(--type-heading-1-line-height);
  }

  .statement-hero p:not(.eyebrow),
  .statement-section p,
  .statement-section li {
    color: var(--colour-text-secondary);
  }

  .statement-hero p:not(.eyebrow) {
    margin-block: 0;
    font-size: var(--type-body-large-font-size);
    line-height: var(--type-body-large-line-height);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-block: 0;
    color: var(--colour-text-muted);
    font-family: var(--type-metadata-font-family);
    font-size: var(--type-metadata-font-size);
    font-weight: var(--type-metadata-font-weight);
    line-height: var(--type-metadata-line-height);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .statement-section {
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--colour-border-subtle);
  }

  .statement-section:last-child {
    border-block-end: 0;
  }

  .statement-section h2 {
    margin-block: 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  .statement-section p,
  .statement-section ul {
    margin-block: 0;
  }

  .statement-section li + li {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
  }

  .action {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-block-size: 44px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-accent-default);
    border-radius: var(--radius-1);
    background-color: var(--colour-accent-default);
    color: var(--colour-text-on-accent);
    font-family: var(--type-label-font-family);
    font-size: var(--type-label-font-size);
    font-weight: var(--type-label-font-weight);
    text-align: center;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition-duration: var(--motion-duration-fast);
    transition-property: background-color, color;
    transition-timing-function: var(--motion-ease-standard);
  }

  .action:hover,
  .action:active {
    background-color: var(--colour-accent-hover);
    color: var(--colour-text-on-accent);
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    :global(#main-content) {
      inline-size: min(
        100% - (2 * var(--layout-gutter-tablet)),
        var(--layout-content-readable)
      );
    }
  }
</style>
